---

## 2. Target Audience

Diamond workers (primarily in Gujarat, India) who need to:
- Log daily diamond polishing/cutting work with quantity and rate per diamond.
- Track monthly earnings, diamond counts, and growth trends.
- Have a simple, fast, offline-ready tool in **Gujarati or English**.

---

## 3. Tech Stack & Infrastructure

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React 19 + Vite 7 |
| Styling | Custom CSS (Glassmorphism, CSS Variables, animations) |
| Backend / DB | Firebase Firestore (NoSQL, cloud-hosted) |
| Authentication | Firebase Auth — **Google Sign-In only** |
| Hosting | Firebase Hosting (CDN) |
| Icons | lucide-react |
| i18n | react-i18next (English + Gujarati) |
| PWA | vite-plugin-pwa + Workbox (offline caching, home screen install) |
| Legacy Support | @vitejs/plugin-legacy (polyfills for older Android/iOS) |

---

## 4. Core Features (for Product Details / User Guide page)

### 4.1 Google Sign-In (Login Screen)
- Single-button Google authentication.
- Language toggle available **before** login (Gujarati ↔ English).
- No email/password option — Google only.
- Each user's data is fully isolated under their Google account.

### 4.2 Dashboard (Home Tab)
- **Current Month Spotlight:** Two premium gradient cards showing:
  - Total Earnings (₹) this month
  - Total Diamonds processed this month
- **Detailed Insights Card** showing:
  - Highest earning day (date + amount)
  - Lowest earning day (date + amount)
  - Growth comparison vs previous month (↑ green / ↓ red)
- **Previous Months:** Compact single-card view for each historical month with all the same metrics inline.
- All dates displayed in **DD/MM/YYYY** format.

### 4.3 New Entry (New Entry Tab)
- Date picker with calendar icon (always shows DD/MM/YYYY).
- Auto-populates rows with user's configured default rates from Settings.
- Each row has: **Rate (₹)** and **Quantity (number of diamonds)**.
- Users can add/remove rows dynamically.
- Auto-calculates subtotals per row and grand total.
- Custom toast notifications for validation warnings and success.
- On save → redirects to History tab with a success animation.

### 4.4 History (History Tab)
- View all past entries filtered by month (horizontal scrollable month pills).
- Sort by: Newest First, Oldest First, Highest Amount, Lowest Amount.
- Each entry card shows:
  - Date (DD/MM/YYYY)
  - Timestamp of when it was recorded
  - Total diamond count
  - Itemized breakdown (quantity × rate = subtotal)
  - Grand total in green
- Delete entries via a confirmation modal (glassmorphism design).

### 4.5 Settings Tab
- **Default Amounts Manager:** Add/remove preset rates (e.g., ₹5, ₹10, ₹15) that auto-fill the New Entry form.
- **Language Toggle:** Switch between English and Gujarati. The choice **persists** across app restarts (saved in localStorage).
- **User Profile:** Shows Google profile photo, name, and email.
- **Logout** button.

### 4.6 PWA / Installability
- Can be installed on phone home screens as a standalone app (no browser chrome).
- Works offline after first load (Workbox service worker caches assets).
- Fast load times via Firebase CDN.

### 4.7 Bilingual Support
- Full Gujarati (ગુજરાતી) and English UI.
- Language can be toggled on the login screen or in Settings.
- Language preference is remembered permanently.

---

## 5. Data Handling & Privacy Details (for Privacy Policy page)

### 5.1 Authentication
- **Method:** Google Sign-In via Firebase Authentication.
- **Data collected at sign-in:** Google display name, email address, profile photo URL.
- **No passwords are stored** — authentication is delegated entirely to Google.

### 5.2 Data Storage
- **Database:** Google Cloud Firestore (Firebase).
- **Data location:** Google Cloud servers (governed by Google Cloud's infrastructure).
- **Data structure:**
  - `users/{userId}/entries/` — each entry stores: date, items (rate, quantity, subtotal per row), total amount, and a server timestamp.
  - `users/{userId}/presets/` — stores the user's default rate presets (rate value + creation timestamp).
- **Data isolation:** Each user can only read/write their own data. Firestore security rules enforce user-level isolation via `auth.uid`.

### 5.3 Data Collected
| Data Type | Purpose | Stored Where |
|---|---|---|
| Google Name, Email, Photo | Display in user profile section | Firebase Auth (Google servers) |
| Diamond work entries (date, rates, quantities, totals) | Core app functionality — tracking earnings | Firestore (Google Cloud) |
| Default rate presets | Pre-fill the entry form | Firestore (Google Cloud) |
| Language preference ([en](file:///Users/kevin/Desktop/Development/Custom%20WebPages/HeeraHisaab/src/components/Dashboard.jsx#13-22) or [gu](file:///Users/kevin/Desktop/Development/Custom%20WebPages/HeeraHisaab/src/components/Login.jsx#26-30)) | Remember UI language choice | Browser localStorage (device only) |

### 5.4 What is NOT Collected
- ❌ No device identifiers or fingerprinting
- ❌ No location data / GPS
- ❌ No contacts or phone data
- ❌ No advertising IDs or ad tracking
- ❌ No third-party analytics (no Google Analytics, no Mixpanel, etc.)
- ❌ No cookies for tracking purposes
- ❌ No data is sold or shared with any third party

### 5.5 Data Retention & Deletion
- User data is retained as long as the user's account exists.
- Users can **delete individual entries** from within the app (History tab → delete button).
- To delete all data and their account, users can contact the developer, or the developer can provide a "Delete Account" feature in a future update.
- If the Firebase project is deleted, all associated data is permanently destroyed.

### 5.6 Third-Party Services
| Service | Provider | Purpose | Their Privacy Policy |
|---|---|---|---|
| Firebase Authentication | Google | User sign-in | https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy |
| Cloud Firestore | Google | Data storage | https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy |
| Firebase Hosting | Google | Serving the web app | https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy |

### 5.7 Security Measures
- All data transmitted over **HTTPS** (TLS encryption in transit).
- Firestore security rules ensure users can only access their own data.
- No sensitive financial data (bank accounts, card numbers) is ever collected.
- The app does not process payments of any kind.

### 5.8 Children's Privacy
- The app is not directed at children under 13.
- No data is knowingly collected from children.

### 5.9 Changes to Privacy Policy
- The developer reserves the right to update the privacy policy.
- Users will be notified of significant changes via the app or the policy page.

### 5.10 Contact
- For privacy questions or data deletion requests, users can contact: **Kevin Suvagiya** via the portfolio website or the provided contact email.

